; beancount reads an option's number with D(): an empty value is 0, commas
; and spaces are dropped, and underscores pass. The last, 10, makes the
; transaction's tolerance 0.1 * 10, so its residual of 0.5 is tolerated.
option "tolerance_multiplier" ""
option "tolerance_multiplier" "1,000"
option "tolerance_multiplier" " 10 "
option "tolerance_multiplier" "1_0"

2020-01-01 open Assets:A
2020-01-01 open Assets:B

2020-01-02 * "Residual within the multiplied tolerance"
  Assets:A   1.0 USD
  Assets:B  -1.5 USD
